{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('map.json'))\nm['surfaces'].append({\\\"entry_point\\\":\\\"state/state.go value and command codec\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"infrastructure\\\",\n \\\"reason\\\":\\\"the value and command wire codecs frame every command a replica sends or receives; they carry no protocol decision, but the direct check for claim C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire confirmed that a value beyond the two-byte length field is silently shortened while its bytes remain in the stream, which the default 1000-byte command size does not reach (S37-state-value-codec, S38-client-command-size).\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\"],\\\"high_consequence\\\":False})\nco=m['core_overview']\nco['open_details'].append(\\\"the command value codec frames a value's length in a two-byte field on both sides, while the client's command size is configuration-driven; the direct check for claim C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire confirmed that a 70000-byte value is written as 70013 bytes but decoded as 4464 bytes with only 4477 bytes consumed, so the value is shortened and the rest of the stream is left for the next message. The default configuration's 1000-byte commands never reach the boundary, and what a replica reader does with the shifted stream is unread (S37-state-value-codec, S38-client-command-size).\\\")\njson.dump(m,open('map.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nfb={\\\"ref_ids\\\":[\\\"4cd03e5aa3ec4080807408f6b3678c14\\\",\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"B15-durable-record\\\"],\n \\\"answered\\\":\\\"The codec truncation is now a confirmed result: the direct check for claim C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire reproduced a 70000-byte value written as 70013 bytes but decoded as 4464 bytes with 4477 consumed. The map records it where the framing lives (a new infrastructure surface for the value and command codec) and as an overview detail that also states the boundary the default configuration stays inside and the unread consequence for a shifted reader stream.\\\",\n \\\"remaining\\\":[\\\"what a replica participant does when its reader is shifted by the leftover bytes, which no check exercised\\\",\n   \\\"whether the client library caps the command size it builds\\\",\n   \\\"the scope-issue bookkeeping on the superseded C1 artifact\\\"],\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The codec is framing infrastructure rather than a protocol decision, so it is recorded as a surface plus an overview detail with the claim and check as the home for the verdict; the two open questions are stated instead of being absorbed, and the default configuration's safety boundary is explicit.\\\",\n \\\"understanding\\\":\\\"updated\\\",\\\"question_updates\\\":{}}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Map handoff for the confirmed codec truncation: one new surface for the value/command codec and one overview open detail, both sourced, with no change to any requirement, binding, edge or identity.\\\",\n \\\"map_path\\\":\\\"map.json\\\",\n \\\"map_changes\\\":{\\\"core_overview\\\":{\\\"impact\\\":\\\"clarification\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"An open detail records the confirmed codec truncation, the configuration boundary that keeps the default deployment inside the field's range, and the unread reader-side consequence.\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\"],\\\"preserves\\\":\\\"Formation, context, connection and the existing open details are unchanged.\\\"}},\n \\\"feedback\\\":fb}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-map-c10.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-map-c10.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
